# Margin

The `margin` MCP server reads ONE project, the one the `MARGIN_INGEST_KEY` belongs to. It
only reads. Never ask the user to paste the key into the chat or write it into a repo file.

**Where the money goes.** Call `margin_jobs` (spend per job over 30 days, model, whether an
eval covers it, concentration), `margin_portfolio_economics` (totals and cost per passed
outcome) and `margin_blind_spots` (what the numbers cannot see, with the fix). Report only
what the tools return. Outcomes are per workflow, so never invent a per-job cost per outcome.
With no customer-supplied value, the figure is cost per outcome; say so.

**What is worth a face-off.** Call `margin_optimize`. Lead with `basis: "measured"` moves,
never present `prior` or `untested` as a saving, and weigh each move by its job's share of
spend from `margin_jobs`. Queueing a face-off spends the project's measurement allowance, so
the user does it in the console at the `queue_in` link. You cannot queue one.

**What the face-offs said.** Call `margin_faceoff_status`: each face-off's status and verdict,
and the post-merge watch (`holds`, `slipped`, `watching`, `not_merged`) on merged changes.
Pull requests and reverts open from https://console.trymargin.io/me, because that click is
the user's approval. Do not reproduce the change by hand to get around it.

**Connecting a project.** OpenRouter users add Margin as a Broadcast destination
(`https://trymargin.io/api/ingest/otlp/v1/traces`, header `Authorization: Bearer <key>`).
Direct SDK users: call `margin_instrument_plan`, make its edits, then run
`python -m margin_meter.doctor --json` (or `npx margin-meter doctor --json`) and report every
gap it lists. Evals: `margin_eval_setup_plan`. Cursor's own usage cannot be metered from a
local file: its OTLP export is set in the Cursor team admin dashboard.

An empty answer means nothing was found, never "all clear".
